         text="Around 1582 Akbar began to admit a circle of courtiers as his personal disciples, bound by vows of loyalty and a few shared practices. Later writers called it Din-i-Ilahi, the divine faith; it was never a mass religion and had perhaps a few dozen members. Where the ceremonies took place is not recorded.",
